+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 placed changing or cancelling a booked visit out of scope, confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08. That ADR also set the only condition under which the row reopens: an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, carrying its own non-goal ADR. The owner made that decision on 2026-08-28. A visit booked with the wrong date or the wrong description has no remedy today, and the record stays wrong.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the row's rationale is visit lifecycle state, and a correction adds none. Forward-only correction is a pattern the sample already demonstrates twice, for owner details and for pet details.
+2. **Open NG-5 entirely.** Build correction and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is exactly the lifecycle state the 2026-08-08 rationale declined. A cancelled visit is a visit in a second state, and nothing else in the sample carries one.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+A booked visit's date and description may be corrected in place, validated on the same terms as booking. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope. NG-4 is untouched: a visit still cannot be deleted.
+
+The correction is reached directly in this decision; no page links to it. Adding a visible entry point is a separate request, not an implied part of this one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 now covers cancellation only, and its rationale names the part that was actually declined rather than a wider row.
+- The sample demonstrates forward-only correction across all three editable records — owner, pet, and visit — and still deletes nothing.
+- Correction is unreachable by navigation until a later request supplies an entry point. The PRD carries this as an open question.
+- The precedent the 2026-08-08 ADR set holds: a non-goal row narrows only by a recorded owner decision, never by implication from a request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the decision this one narrows.
